{#
  The configuration as it is in Mongo: what is running, read.

  One page: the general matters, the providers, then one section per subsystem.
  The template prints what src/view.js worked out — it walks, it does not compute:
  no arithmetic, no decision about what a value means.

  **Nothing is configured here.** The providers are listed with the price of their
  tokens as it is stored; writing one is another page, `/providers/pricing`, and
  this one links to it. A page that shows the configuration and a page that
  changes it are two different things to be looking at, and a form in the middle
  of a reading is a click away from a write nobody meant.

  The shell and the macro that prints a value are shared with that other page:
  `layout.njk` and `value.njk`.

  Expected: view (src/view.js buildView).
#}{% extends "layout.njk" %}
{% import "value.njk" as show %}

{% block nav %}
<nav class="index">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a href="#general">general matters</a>
    <a href="#providers">providers</a>
    {%- for subsystem in view.subsystems %}
    <a href="#{{ subsystem.anchor }}">{{ subsystem.name }}</a>
    {%- endfor %}
    <a class="elsewhere" href="/providers/pricing">providers' prices →</a>
  </div>
</nav>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  {%- if view.failure %}
  <section class="failure">
    <h2>The configuration was not read</h2>
    <p class="detail">{{ view.failure }}</p>
    <p>Nothing below it is shown. The page reads anagraphics, which serves what is in Mongo.</p>
  </section>
  {%- endif %}

  <section id="general">
    <h2>General matters</h2>

    <h3>Bootstrap</h3>
    <p class="note">The <code>WEBTOOLS_*</code> variables this process received. They are not
      configuration: they are what reaches it. Their source is
      <code>webtools/configurator/bootstrap.env</code>.</p>
    {%- if view.bootstrap.length %}
    <table class="grid">
      <tbody>
        {%- for variable in view.bootstrap %}
        <tr><th>{{ variable.name }}</th><td><span class="value string">{{ variable.value }}</span></td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {%- else %}
    <p class="absent">No <code>WEBTOOLS_*</code> variable in this process's environment.</p>
    {%- endif %}

    <h3>Subsystems</h3>
    {%- if view.subsystems.length %}
    <table class="grid">
      <thead><tr><th>subsystem</th><th>listens on</th><th>fields</th><th>secret</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for subsystem in view.subsystems %}
        <tr>
          <td><a href="#{{ subsystem.anchor }}">{{ subsystem.name }}</a></td>
          <td>{% if subsystem.listen %}<span class="value string">{{ subsystem.listen }}</span>{% else %}<span class="absent">—</span>{% endif %}</td>
          <td class="number-cell">{{ subsystem.leaves }}</td>
          <td class="number-cell">{% if subsystem.secrets %}{{ subsystem.secrets }}{% else %}<span class="absent">—</span>{% endif %}</td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {%- elif not view.failure %}
    <p class="absent">The <code>configuration</code> collection holds no document.</p>
    {%- endif %}

    <h3>Shared values</h3>
    <p class="note">Leaves that more than one subsystem holds with the same value. A path held with
      different values is not here: that is a divergence, not a shared value.</p>
    {%- if view.shared.length %}
    <table class="grid">
      <thead><tr><th>path</th><th>value</th><th>in</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for entry in view.shared %}
        <tr>
          <th>{{ entry.path }}</th>
          <td>{{ show.value(entry.value) }}</td>
          <td class="who">{% for name in entry.subsystems %}<span class="item">{{ name }}</span>{% endfor %}</td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {%- else %}
    <p class="absent">No leaf is held with the same value by more than one subsystem.</p>
    {%- endif %}

    <h3>Secrets</h3>
    {%- if view.secrets.available %}
    <p class="note">A field is shown as <span class="value secret">(secret)</span> when it comes from
      <code>webtools/configurator/secrets/</code>, which <code>load_configuration.sh</code>
      deep-merges into the configuration. The values are not read by this page.</p>
    {%- else %}
    <p class="warning">The secrets folder was not read: <code>{{ view.secrets.reason }}</code>.
      No field is marked as secret — which does not mean there are none in Mongo.</p>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if view.secrets.problems.length %}
    <ul class="warning">
      {%- for problem in view.secrets.problems %}
      <li>{{ problem }}</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if view.secrets.orphans.length %}
    <p class="warning">Secrets files with no configuration to merge into:
      {% for name in view.secrets.orphans %}<code>{{ name }}</code>{% endfor %}.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </section>


  <section id="providers">
    <h2>Providers</h2>
    <p class="note">One row per <strong>door</strong>: a place where a subsystem asks a model of a
      provider. A door is an object hanging from a <code>providers</code> branch that names a
      <code>model</code>, wherever in the document that branch is. The list comes out of the
      documents, so a door added tomorrow is here.</p>
    <p class="note">An object under a <code>providers</code> branch that names no model is not a
      door and is not here: nothing is asked of a provider through it. What it is, is what its own
      fields say — <code>token_kinds</code> declares which kinds of token that provider counts —
      and it is read in its subsystem's section below, with the rest of that document.</p>
    <p class="note">The price is the price of what that door's model consumes: one amount per kind
      of token, in hundredths of the currency's unit, per million tokens. It is shown here as it is
      stored. To write one: <a href="/providers/pricing">providers' prices</a>.</p>
    {%- if view.providers.length %}
    <table class="grid">
      <thead><tr><th>provider</th><th>in</th><th>model</th><th>price</th><th>last written</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {%- for entry in view.providers %}
        {%- for door in entry.doors %}
        <tr>
          <th>{{ entry.provider }}</th>
          <td><a href="#{{ door.subsystemAnchor }}"><code>{{ door.subsystem }}</code></a> <code class="path">{{ door.path }}</code></td>
          <td>
            {%- if door.modelIsSecret %}<span class="value secret">(secret)</span>
            {%- else %}<span class="value string">{{ door.model }}</span>{% endif %}
          </td>
          <td>
            {%- if door.rows.length %}<span class="value list">{% for row in door.rows %}<span class="item">{{ row.kind }} {{ row.text }}{% if door.currency %} {{ door.currency }}{% endif %}</span>{% endfor %}</span>
            {%- else %}<span class="absent">—</span>{% endif %}
          </td>
          <td>{% if door.updatedAt %}<span class="updated">{{ door.updatedAt }}</span>{% else %}<span class="absent">never</span>{% endif %}</td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {%- elif not view.failure %}
    <p class="absent">No subsystem asks a model of a provider.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </section>

  {%- for subsystem in view.subsystems %}
  <section id="{{ subsystem.anchor }}">
    <h2>{{ subsystem.name }}</h2>
    <p class="meta">
      {% if subsystem.listen %}listens on {{ subsystem.listen }} · {% endif %}{{ subsystem.leaves }} fields{% if subsystem.secrets %} · {{ subsystem.secrets }} secret{% endif %}
    </p>
    {%- if subsystem.secretsNotInMongo.length %}
    <p class="warning">Declared in the secrets file and not in Mongo:
      {% for path in subsystem.secretsNotInMongo %}<code>{{ path }}</code>{% endfor %}.
      Usually <code>load_configuration.sh</code> has not been run since the file was written.</p>
    {%- endif %}
    <div class="tree">
      {%- for row in subsystem.rows %}
      <div class="row {{ row.kind }}" style="--depth: {{ row.depth }}">
        <span class="key">{{ row.key }}</span>
        {%- if row.kind == "branch" %}
        <span class="size">{{ row.size }}</span>
        {%- else %}
        {{ show.value(row.value) }}
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}
{% endblock %}

{% block footer %}
    <p>Read-only. The configuration that lives is in Mongo; the files in
      <code>webtools/configurator/configuration/</code> are the seed. The one value written from the configurator's front end is the price of a provider's
      tokens, on its own page: <a href="/providers/pricing">providers' prices</a>. To change any
      other:
      edit the file and run <code>webtools/configurator/load_configuration.sh</code>, which adds
      only the missing fields, then restart whoever reads it.</p>
{% endblock %}
